  "notes": [
    "New tax regime under section 115BAC(1A) of the Income-tax Act, 1961, for assessment year 2026-27.",
    "Old tax regime for an individual below 60: slabs nil up to ₹2,50,000, 5%, 20% above ₹5,00,000 and 30% above ₹10,00,000; standard deduction ₹50,000; section 87A rebate up to ₹12,500 when total income is at most ₹5,00,000; surcharge up to 37% above ₹5 crore. Section 80C is capped at ₹1,50,000 and section 80D at ₹1,00,000 (the most possible: ₹50,000 for self and family plus ₹50,000 for parents, both senior citizens).",
    "Tax year 2026-27 (from 1 April 2026, Income-tax Act, 2025) keeps the same slabs, surcharge and cess per the Finance Bill 2026 memorandum; it will be added once the standard deduction and rebate under the 2025 Act are verified from the Act itself."
